      "text": "Cottingham formula for the electromagnetic self-energy contribution to Mp − Mn — 5 sections: Front matter; Introduction; The Cottingham Formula\n\n**Cottingham formula for the electromagnetic self-energy contribution to Mp − Mn**\n\n*André Walker-Loud∗*\n\n7 pp, 5 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 The Cottingham Formula; 4 Concluding Remarks; References\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Proposition: At LO, lattice QCD can be used to reliably compute the contribution from md −mu.\n- Proposition: (1.3) Calculating δMγ with lattice QCD and QED is much more challenging, due to the disparate length scales relevant for the two theories.\n- Proposition: (1.4) If we instead subtract the lattice QCD determination from experiment, we arrive at δMp−n −δMmd−mu LQCD = 1.24(40) MeV.\n- Proposition: We report on an effort to improve the electromagnetic self-energy contribution using the Cottingham Formula [1].\n- Proposition: The Cottingham Formula The Cottingham Formula intuitively relates the electromagnetic self-energy to forward Comp- ton Scattering (see Fig.\n- Proposition: 2 Cottingham Formula André Walker-Loud µ ν p p q q (a) (b) Figure 1: The Cottingham Formula intuitively relates the forward Compton Scattering (a) to the O(αf.s.) electromagnetic",
